%% title: Firmware MQTT session lifecycle
%% source: firmware/esp32_feeder/net.cpp:81-106 retry, will, birth, subscribe
%% source: firmware/esp32_feeder/net.cpp:135-136 buffer 1024 and keepalive 60

sequenceDiagram
  participant ESP as ESP32
  participant B as Broker
  participant PL as Platform

  ESP->>B: CONNECT clientId feeder-64008c, keepalive 60 s, socket timeout 10 s
  Note over ESP,B: will topic feeder-ayurahmaw/feeder-64008c/status, payload offline, QoS 0, retain true
  B-->>ESP: CONNACK accepted
  ESP->>B: publish status online, retain true, QoS 0
  B-->>PL: status online, worker sets is_online 1
  PL->>PL: resolve device_offline notification
  ESP->>B: subscribe command topic at QoS 1
  B-->>ESP: SUBACK granted QoS 1
  Note over ESP: other topics are ignored, the embedded broker may replay retained ones

  loop while the session is up
    ESP->>B: publish telemetry every 15000 ms
    ESP->>B: PINGREQ, keepalive period 60 s
    B-->>ESP: PINGRESP
  end

  Note over ESP,B: WiFi drops or the board loses power, so no clean DISCONNECT is sent
  B-->>PL: will published, status offline retained
  PL->>PL: handle_status offline, insert device_offline warning
  Note over PL: the sweeper also flags the device after 45 s without telemetry

  loop every 5000 ms while WiFi is down
    ESP->>ESP: WiFi reconnect and client connect retry
  end
  ESP->>B: CONNECT again, same clientId and same will
  B-->>ESP: CONNACK accepted
  ESP->>B: publish status online retained, birth message again
  ESP->>B: publish telemetry immediately on the rising edge
  B-->>PL: status online, device_offline resolved
